itecture-4","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"USDZ loading (`apps/web/src/viewer/usd/`)"},"7":{"id":"/docs/architecture-5","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"`bike-scene/1` (viewer JSON, `*.bike.json`)"},"8":{"id":"/docs/architecture-6","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"Photo close-ups"},"9":{"id":"/docs/architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"Open questions (verify on device)"},"10":{"id":"/docs/architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#why-object-capture-instead-of-wes-bos-room-pipeline","content":"`wesbos/3d-model-anything` records RoomPlan + LiDAR mesh + posed photos, then an AI agent\nrebuilds the room in three.js. A bike is one object with thin tubes, spokes and cables, so we\nuse Apple's Object Capture: guided orbits, **automatic object masking** (the background is\nremoved during reconstruction; no green screen needed) and a textured USDZ. We keep Wes's\nkey idea of **posed photos**: `poses.json` tells us where each photo was taken, so the viewer\ncan show real close-up photos for an area (e.g. the fork crown) next to the 3D view."},"11":{"id":"/docs/architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#why-object-capture-instead-of-wes-bos-room-pipeline","content":"Fallbacks when Object Capture struggles with a bike (thin spokes are the classic failure):\narea mode + a crop box, or a gaussian splat (Scaniverse/Polycam/Luma) for photoreal paint.\nThe green background mode exists for compositing snapshots/videos in other tools."},"12":{"id":"/docs/architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"| Path            | Content                                                                                                        |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `manifest.json` | `{ schema, name, createdAt, device, systemVersion, mode: \"object\"\\|\"area\", model, poses, images, imageCount }` |","table":"table-0"},"13":{"id":"/docs/architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"| Path         | Content                       |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| `model.usdz` | reconstruction, meters, +Y up |","table":"table-0"},"14":{"id":"/docs/architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"| Path         | Content                                                                                              |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `poses.json` | `{ schema: \"bike-poses/1\", samples: [{ sample, file, transform[16] }] }` (column-major camera→model) |","table":"table-0"},"15":{"id":"/docs/architecture-13","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"| Path      | Content                    |\n| --------- | -------------------------- |\n| `images/` | Object Capture HEIC photos |","table":"table-0"},"16":{"id":"/docs/architecture-14","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"| Path          | Content             |\n| ------------- | ------------------- |\n| `record.json` | app-internal record |","table":"table-0"},"17":{"id":"/docs/architecture-15","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"Importing in the browser (`apps/web/src/scene/capture.ts`): dropping a `*.bikecapture.zip`\nunzips it in memory with fflate; nothing is uploaded. The iOS exporter zips its staging folder\n(`NSFileCoordinator .forUploading`), so files usually sit under one top-level directory: the\nshallowest `manifest.json` defines the bundle root and `__MACOSX/` / `._*` entries are ignored.\nOnly `manifest.json`, the model and `poses.json` are decompressed (size-capped); images are just\nlisted. If `manifest.model` is missing, a `glb`/`gltf`/`usdz`/`ply` next to the manifest is used\n(GLB first, e.g. after `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`). A broken `poses.json` is a warning, not an error."},"18":{"id":"/docs/architecture-16","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-capture1-ios-export-zip","content":"The resulting scene gets a stable id (`capture-<name>-<createdAt digits>`) so dropping the same\nbundle again restores its saved areas and comments, and a model URL `bundle:<zip name>/<path>`,\nwhich is never fetched: it is resolved from memory or from the capture cache below, and only\nwhen neither has it does the viewer ask for that zip to be dropped again."},"19":{"id":"/docs/architecture-17","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"So a capture scene survives a reload, every successfully opened bundle is kept in the browser\n(`apps/web/src/scene/captureCache.ts`, pure logic; `apps/web/src/storage/backends.ts`, storage):"},"20":{"id":"/docs/architecture-18","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**What**: the model bytes, `manifest.json`, `poses.json` and the image list. Lazily extracted\nfiles (photos, thumbnails) can be added to an entry later (`putFile`) and are evicted with it.\nThe zip itself is not kept (HEIC photos make it hundreds of MB)."},"21":{"id":"/docs/architecture-19","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**Where**: OPFS (`navigator.storage.getDirectory()`, folder `bike-captures/`, flat\npercent-encoded file names), falling back to IndexedDB (`bike-3d-brew` / `files`) when OPFS is\nmissing, has no `createWritable()` (older Safari) or refuses a probe write. Neither → no cache,\nthe old \"drop the zip again\" behavior. `navigator.storage.persist()` is requested once per page\nload, on the first store."},"22":{"id":"/docs/architecture-20","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**Keys**: one entry per `bundle:` model URL; files live under `cap-<slug>-<fnv1a(url)>/…` and an\n`index.json` lists entries (validated on read). An entry remembers the scene id it was opened\nas, so a different bike exported with the same zip filename never loads the wrong model."},"23":{"id":"/docs/architecture-21","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**Budget**: LRU by last use, `min(500 MB, 50% of the quota − other usage)` from\n`navigator.storage.estimate()`. A bundle larger than the whole budget is simply not cached."},"24":{"id":"/docs/architecture-22","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**Failure**: every call is best effort. Any storage error leaves the app as if the cache did\nnot exist; entries whose files vanished (browser eviction) are dropped from the index."},"25":{"id":"/docs/architecture-23","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#capture-cache-browser-storage","content":"**UI**: \"Open…\" becomes a small menu once something is stored: \"Choose a file…\" plus the stored\ncaptures (name, size, × to forget)."},"26":{"id":"/docs/architecture-24","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"Object Capture writes a USDZ whose root layer is **binary USDC (crate)**: one baked triangle\nmesh, indexed face-varying `primvars:st` and normals, a `UsdPreviewSurface` fed by\n`UsdUVTexture` PNGs in `0/` (diffuse, normal with scale 2 / bias -1, occlusion),\n`metersPerUnit = 1`, `upAxis = \"Y\"`."},"27":{"id":"/docs/architecture-25","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"three.js r186 can read this: `USDLoader` (the old `USDZLoader` is a deprecated alias) has a crate\nparser with LZ4 + integer decoding (`usd/USDCParser.js`) and a composer that handles xforms,\nGeomSubsets, indexed/face-varying primvars, UsdPreviewSurface textures, `metersPerUnit` and Z-up.\nWe reuse those parsers and patch what fails on real-world files:"},"28":{"id":"/docs/architecture-26","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"`crate.ts` (`CrateParser`): values the crate stores **inline** that r186 misreads: small integral\n`double2/3/4` and `half3/4` (packed int8, e.g. `xformOp:translate = (0, 0, 5)` became a number and\ncrashed the transform), negative `int`, `half`; plus scalar `half3/4`, `quath`, `int4`, `matrix2d/3d`."},"29":{"id":"/docs/architecture-27","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"`composer.ts` (`FastUSDComposer`): typed-array fast path for all-triangle meshes. Stock three took\n~1.4–2.2 s to build a 1M-triangle mesh (JS arrays per index); this takes ~0.2 s, same output."},"30":{"id":"/docs/architecture-28","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"`usdz.ts` (`loadUsd`): unzips only USD layers and images, takes the first layer as root (falls back\nto the first USD layer anywhere), composes, waits for textures (blob URLs created and revoked by\nthree per image), halves three's normal-map strength for the standard scale 2 / bias -1 decode,\nand reports undecodable textures as warnings instead of failing."},"31":{"id":"/docs/architecture-29","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#usdz-loading-appswebsrcviewerusd","content":"Measured on a synthetic 23 MB USDZ (972k triangles, 2048² texture; `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py\n--detail 90 --tex 2048`), Chromium: unzip 16 ms, parse 183 ms, build 206 ms, textures 24 ms. Parsing\nstays on the main thread: a worker would save the ~0.2 s parse but pay ~0.07 s structured-clone of\nthe spec table back, and the build step needs three.js objects on the main thread anyway. The USD\ncode (~70 KB min) is a lazy chunk loaded on the first USDZ. Anything that still fails shows an error\npointing to `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`. Fixtures are synthetic (`apps/web/test/fixtures/README.md`)."},"32":{"id":"/docs/architecture-30","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#bike-scene1-viewer-json-bikejson","content":"See `apps/web/src/scene/schema.ts`. A scene references its model by URL (relative to the\nscene file), lists **hotspots** (named camera views: the zoomable areas) and **annotations**\n(surface point + normal, title, body, kind `feature|spec|upgrade|note`, optional price and area).\nAll coordinates are in model-root space."},"33":{"id":"/docs/architecture-31","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"For the active area (its view target, preferring cameras on the side its saved view looks from),\nthe active comment (its pin, preferring cameras in front of its surface normal) and each Present\nstep, the viewer shows a filmstrip of the capture photos that best show that point; tapping one\nopens a full-screen viewer (arrows / swipe, pinch / wheel / double-tap zoom, Esc)."},"34":{"id":"/docs/architecture-32","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"**Spaces.** A pose is a column-major camera→reconstruction matrix, camera looking down -Z,\n+Y up. Scene positions are in model-root space. `Viewer.setModel` adds `centerOnGround(object)`\nto the model root, so `modelRoot ⟵ reconstruction` is the loaded object's local matrix (the\ncentering shift plus any root transform the loader applied) times the identity wrapper:\n`src/viewer/captureSpace.ts`. The scene's `model.rotation/scale/offset` sit on the model root\nitself and never enter the mapping. A unit test runs the fixture USDZ through three's\n`USDLoader` + `centerOnGround` and checks the expected close-ups win."},"35":{"id":"/docs/architecture-33","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"**Ranking** (`src/scene/photos.ts`, pure): keep photos whose frustum contains the target\n(assumed iPhone wide camera, 65° × 51°, landscape sensor; poses carry no intrinsics), drop\ncameras behind the surface (`side` hint), score `0.45·centered + 0.35·closeness + 0.2·facing`\n(closeness relative to the nearest usable photo, so units do not matter), and skip near-duplicate\nviewpoints. Occlusion is not tested."},"36":{"id":"/docs/architecture-34","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#photo-close-ups","content":"**Photos** (`src/ui/photoLibrary.ts`): extracted one at a time from the dropped zip via its\ncentral directory (`src/scene/zipIndex.ts`: the `File` stays on disk, nothing else is inflated),\ndecoded natively (`createImageBitmap`, then `<img>`; Safari reads HEIC), else HEIC goes to a\nmodule worker that lazily loads libheif (`libheif-js`, WASM, ~2 MB, LGPL-3.0, only fetched when a\nHEIC photo is shown). Results are downscaled to JPEG (360 px thumbnails, 2048 px full) and added\nto the capture cache entry, so after a reload the photos already seen still show without the zip."},"37":{"id":"/docs/architecture-35","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"Does `PhotogrammetrySession.Poses` return camera→model transforms in the same frame as the\nUSDZ? (Assumed, and the photo close-ups depend on it; validate by checking that an area's top\nclose-up really shows that area on a real capture.)"},"38":{"id":"/docs/architecture-36","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"~~Does three.js read Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC)?~~ Yes, with the fixes above, verified on\nsynthetic Object-Capture-like files. Still to confirm on a real capture (docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md)."},"39":{"id":"/docs/architecture-37","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"Bike size vs. Object Capture's bounding box limits: area mode is the fallback."},"40":{"id":"/docs/architecture-38","page_id":"/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/architecture#open-questions-verify-on-device","content":"_Source: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`_"},"41":{"id":"/docs/changelog","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"page","content":"Changelog","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Plan"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog"},"42":{"id":"/docs/changelog-0","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"Unreleased"},"43":{"id":"/docs/changelog-1","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Added"},"44":{"id":"/docs/changelog-2","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog","content":"Every PR adds a line under **Unreleased** (newest first) with its PR number. When the owner\nmerges the stack to `main`, the Unreleased block becomes a dated release."},"45":{"id":"/docs/changelog-3","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Test system: Playwright E2E suite (`npm run e2e`, desktop + iPhone viewport, sharded CI job) over the production build, covering every viewer flow including stored captures, photo close-ups and binary USDC; synthetic capture-bundle fixtures (`tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`, rendered-photo bundle via `render-photos.mjs`); unit coverage with ratcheting thresholds (`npm run test:coverage`, ~99.8% lines) incl. zip64 parsing, OPFS/IndexedDB backends and the photo UI; `docs/TESTING.md`. UI decisions moved into tested `scene/helpers.ts`; `?e2e` test hook. Fixed: a tap right after an instant (reduced-motion) fly-to missed the model. (#7)"},"46":{"id":"/docs/changelog-4","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Photo close-ups: for the active area, the active comment and each Present step, a filmstrip of the capture photos that best show it (ranked from `poses.json`), with a full-screen viewer (swipe, arrows, pinch/zoom). Photos are read lazily from the zip, HEIC is decoded natively or by a lazily loaded WASM worker, and thumbnails are kept in the capture cache. (#6)"},"47":{"id":"/docs/changelog-5","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Captures survive reloads: opened `*.bikecapture.zip` bundles are kept in browser storage (OPFS, IndexedDB fallback, LRU under a quota-aware budget) and reopen automatically; \"Open…\" lists stored captures with size and a forget button. Synthetic fixture generator in `tools/fixtures/`. (#5)"},"48":{"id":"/docs/changelog-6","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Docs & progress site (Fumadocs, `apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown: home dashboard with roadmap progress per milestone, latest changes and build commit; \"How to test\" guide; offline search. `tools/publish-pages.sh` publishes it with the viewer (under `/app/`) and a synthetic test bundle to the `gh-pages` branch; `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` writes a synthetic `*.bikecapture.zip`. The Actions-based `pages.yml` deploy is removed. (#4)"},"49":{"id":"/docs/changelog-7","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"USDZ robustness: Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC) loads with textures; fixes three.js r186 crate decoding of inline vectors/halves/negative ints, ~10× faster mesh build for large captures, lazy-loaded USD code, clear fallback to `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`. Synthetic fixture generator `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`. (#3)"},"50":{"id":"/docs/changelog-8","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Capture bundle import: drop an iPhone `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer; it is unzipped in the browser, the model loads and the scene is named from the manifest. Re-dropping a bundle restores its comments. (#2)"},"51":{"id":"/docs/changelog-9","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Foundation: three.js viewer/editor with areas, pinned sales comments, present mode, background modes, `bike-scene/1` format; iOS Object Capture app skeleton; CI. (#1)"},"52":{"id":"/docs/changelog-10","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"_Source: `CHANGELOG.md`_"},"53":{"id":"/docs/goals","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"page","content":"Goals","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Plan"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals"},"54":{"id":"/docs/goals-0","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals#product","content":"Product"},"55":{"id":"/docs/goals-1","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"Success criteria"},"56":{"id":"/docs/goals-2","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"Quality bar for every PR"},"57":{"id":"/docs/goals-3","page_id":"/docs/goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/goals#non-goals-for-now","content":"Non-goals (for now)"},"58":{"id":"/docs/goals-4","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#product","content":"A bike shop captures a bike with an iPhone in a few minutes and gets a background-free,\nphotoreal 3D model that sales staff (in store, on a tablet) and customers (on a shared link)\ncan spin, zoom into named areas (fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and read pinned sales comments."},"59":{"id":"/docs/goals-5","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Capture → viewer in under 15 minutes** with no desktop software: capture on iPhone,\nAirDrop the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer."},"60":{"id":"/docs/goals-6","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Looks like the real bike**: textures, thin parts (spokes, cables) acceptable; background gone."},"61":{"id":"/docs/goals-7","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Fast on phones**: first model visible in < 3 s on iPhone Safari over 4G for a 20 MB model;\n60 fps orbiting with 50 pins."},"62":{"id":"/docs/goals-8","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Selling tool, not a 3D toy**: areas and comments are the primary UI; present mode is\nusable by a non-technical salesperson with one hand."},"63":{"id":"/docs/goals-9","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#success-criteria","content":"**Robust**: untrusted files never crash the app; every failure says what to do next."},"64":{"id":"/docs/goals-10","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"Pure logic in `apps/web/src/scene/` with unit tests; coverage does not go down."},"65":{"id":"/docs/goals-11","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"`npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build` and the E2E suite pass; CI green."},"66":{"id":"/docs/goals-12","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"UI changes verified in Chromium with screenshots, at desktop and phone sizes."},"67":{"id":"/docs/goals-13","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#quality-bar-for-every-pr","content":"Docs (ROADMAP, CHANGELOG, ARCHITECTURE, guides) updated in the same PR."},"68":{"id":"/docs/goals-14","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#non-goals-for-now","content":"Public release / app store distribution (the owner decides when)."},"69":{"id":"/docs/goals-15","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#non-goals-for-now","content":"Real customer captures in the repo: only generated fixtures."},"70":{"id":"/docs/goals-16","page_id":"/docs/goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/goals#non-goals-for-now","content":"_Source: `docs/GOALS.md`_"},"71":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"72":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Capture bikes with an iPhone, show them as background-free 3D models, zoom into components\n(fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and pin sales comments on them."},"73":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"**`apps/ios`**: iPhone capture app (Apple Object Capture: background removed automatically, on-device 3D build, camera poses, shareable bundle)."},"74":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"**`apps/web`**: three.js viewer and editor: clear / chroma-green / studio backgrounds, fly-to areas, comment pins, presentation mode, JSON export."},"75":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Drop a `.bikecapture.zip` from the iPhone app (or a `.glb`, `.usdz`, `.ply`) onto the viewer to use your own capture. Switch to **Edit** to\ntap the bike and add comments, save camera views as areas; **Present** steps through areas for\na customer."},"76":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, ROADMAP.md and\napps/ios/README.md. Inspired by\nwesbos/3d-model-anything."},"77":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"_Source: `README.md`_"},"78":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","type":"page","content":"Manual steps","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/manual-steps"},"79":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-0","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"Things an agent cannot do (hardware, accounts, decisions). Newest first."},"80":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-1","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Decide on the HEIC decoder license**: photo close-ups decode HEIC in Chrome/Firefox with\n`libheif-js` (LGPL-3.0), shipped as a separate, lazily loaded worker chunk. Fine for a private\ntool; before a public release, either confirm LGPL compliance (unmodified library in its own\nfile, notice in the about/credits) or remove it once the iOS app exports JPEGs (see ROADMAP)."},"81":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-2","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Close-ups on a real capture**: open a real `.bikecapture.zip` with a few areas and check that\neach area's first photos really show it, in Chrome (WASM HEIC path) and iPhone Safari (native)."},"82":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-3","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Real Object Capture USDZ in the viewer** (needs a real capture): drop the `model.usdz` (or\nthe `.bikecapture.zip`) on the viewer and compare with Quick Look on the Mac/iPhone: textures\npresent and not flipped, size in meters, bike upright, normal-map bumps not exaggerated. The\nbrowser console logs `USDZ …: N triangles, unzip/parse/build ms`; note those numbers in the\nPR. If anything is off, describe the file structure (`usdcat model.usdz | head -80` without\nsharing the capture) so an agent can re-create it in `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`."},"83":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-4","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**Real iPhone capture test** (needs an iPhone with LiDAR, iOS 18+): build `apps/ios`, capture a\nbike, export the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer. Report whether the USDZ loads."},"84":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-5","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"**GitHub Pages**: done by the owner on 2026-10-27 (Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch\n`gh-pages`). The site is published from this repo by `tools/publish-pages.sh`."},"85":{"id":"/docs/manual-steps-6","page_id":"/docs/manual-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/manual-steps","content":"_Source: `docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md`_"},"86":{"id":"/docs/progress","page_id":"/docs/progress","type":"page","content":"Progress","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/progress"},"87":{"id":"/docs/progress-0","page_id":"/docs/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/progress","content":"Roadmap status per milestone, generated from ROADMAP.md at build time."},"88":{"id":"/docs/roadmap","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"page","content":"Roadmap","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Plan"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap"},"89":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-0","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"Milestone 0: Project ops"},"90":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-1","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Milestone 1: Foundation (PR 1)"},"91":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-2","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"Milestone 2: Real captures into the viewer"},"92":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-3","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"Milestone 3: Sales experience"},"93":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-4","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"Milestone 4: iOS app depth"},"94":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-5","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"Milestone 5: Backend & multi-bike catalog"},"95":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-6","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"Milestone 6: Quality"},"96":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-7","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"Ideas parking lot"},"97":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-8","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap","content":"The backlog autonomous sessions work through, top to bottom. Each item is sized for one\nsession / one PR. Protocol is in CLAUDE.md."},"98":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-9","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap","content":"Markers: `[ ]` open · `[~]` in progress (draft PR open) · `[x]` done (in an open or merged PR)."},"99":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-10","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[x] **Docs & progress site**: Fumadocs static site (`apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown, with a roadmap progress dashboard and a \"How to test\" guide, published with the viewer to GitHub Pages by `tools/publish-pages.sh` (site at `/bike-3d-brew/`, viewer at `/bike-3d-brew/app/`)."},"100":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-11","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[ ] **Auto-publish on develop**: a workflow (`contents: write`) that runs `tools/publish-pages.sh --source develop` on every push to `develop`, so the site stays current even when no agent session runs."},"101":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-12","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-0-project-ops","content":"[ ] **PR previews**: publish each open stack PR under `/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (docs + viewer) and link them from the Progress page, so the owner can test a PR before merging it."},"102":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-13","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Web viewer: three.js, orbit, fly-to areas, background modes (clear / chroma green / studio / dark)"},"103":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-14","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Scene format `bike-scene/1` with validation, local persistence, import/export"},"104":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-15","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Areas (hotspots) and sales comments pinned to the model surface, edit + present modes"},"105":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-16","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"Procedural demo bike with seeded areas and comments"},"106":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-17","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"iOS app skeleton: Object Capture (object + area mode), on-device reconstruction, poses, bundle export"},"107":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-18","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-1-foundation-pr-1","content":"CI: web typecheck/test/build, unsigned iOS build on macOS, Pages deploy workflow"},"108":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-19","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Capture bundle import**: drop `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer, unzip in the browser (fflate), load `model.usdz`, read `manifest.json` and `poses.json`, name the scene from the manifest. Unit-test the bundle parser with a synthetic zip."},"109":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-20","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Keep captures across reloads**: cache the unzipped model of the last opened bundles in IndexedDB/OPFS (best effort, quota-aware) so a reload reopens a capture scene without re-dropping the `.bikecapture.zip`."},"110":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-21","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Capture cache on real Safari / iOS**: verify OPFS `createWritable()` vs. the IndexedDB fallback, quota numbers and `persist()` behavior on iPhone Safari and a home-screen web app; tune the 500 MB budget for phones."},"111":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-22","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Cache large models without a main-thread copy**: write models to OPFS from a worker (`createSyncAccessHandle`) or straight from the dropped `File` stream, so a 300 MB capture does not briefly double memory on phones."},"112":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-23","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **USDZ robustness**: three r186 reads binary USDC; `apps/web/src/viewer/usd/` fixes its inline-value decoding, speeds up large meshes ~10×, waits for packed textures and falls back to a `tools/usdz-to-glb.py` hint. Synthetic Object-Capture-like fixtures from `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`."},"113":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-24","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Verify a real Object Capture USDZ**: load a real `model.usdz` (owner's iPhone, see docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md), compare against Quick Look; turn anything off into a fixture-based test (synthetic re-creation, never the capture itself)."},"114":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-25","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Weld USDZ meshes**: three expands face-varying meshes to 3 vertices per triangle (~3M vertices for a 1M-triangle capture); merge identical corners into an indexed geometry to cut GPU memory, and consider decimating for phones."},"115":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-26","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Auto-orient captures**: detect the ground plane / longest horizontal axis so a scanned bike stands upright facing +X; expose rotate/scale/offset controls in Edit mode (writes `model.rotation/scale/offset`)."},"116":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-27","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Crop box for area-mode / splat captures**: draggable box in Edit mode that clips everything outside (clipping planes), saved in the scene, so area-mode scans get a clean background."},"117":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-28","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[x] **Photo close-ups per area**: use `poses.json` to find the capture photos that look most directly at each area target (angle + distance score) and show them as a filmstrip under the area; tap to open full screen. HEIC → JPEG conversion at export time on iOS if browsers can't decode HEIC."},"118":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-29","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **iOS JPEG photo export**: write `images/*.jpg` (or a `photos/` folder of 2048 px JPEGs) next to the HEICs in the bundle so Chrome/Firefox skip the 2 MB WASM HEIC decoder and decoding is instant; the web side already prefers whatever decodes natively."},"119":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-30","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Validate close-ups on a real capture**: confirm Object Capture poses share the USDZ frame and the 65° landscape intrinsics assumption (portrait captures, EXIF rotation); read real intrinsics if the iOS app can export them."},"120":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-31","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Occlusion-aware close-ups**: raycast from each candidate camera to the target against the loaded mesh and drop photos where the bike hides it."},"121":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-32","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-2-real-captures-into-the-viewer","content":"[ ] **Pin favourite close-ups**: let staff star photos for an area (the schema already has `Hotspot.photos`) and show starred ones first, also in shared links."},"122":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-33","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Shareable read-only link**: `?scene=` URL loads a published scene in Present mode with editing hidden; \"Copy share link\" button. Scenes + models served from `apps/web/public/scenes/<id>/`."},"123":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-34","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Comment polish**: leader lines from pin to card in Present mode, auto-advance/kiosk mode, comment ordering (drag to reorder), markdown-lite (bold, bullet lists) in bodies."},"124":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-35","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Hotspot auto-suggest**: for captures, propose default areas (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit, Wheels, Saddle) by letting the user tap each part once; camera view computed from tapped point + local bounds."},"125":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-36","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Spec sheet**: per-bike key specs table (frame material, groupset, weight, sizes) shown in Present mode intro and exported."},"126":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-37","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Branding**: shop logo, accent color and font in scene settings; applied to Present mode."},"127":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-38","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Snapshot / video export**: high-res PNG with transparent or green background; 360° turntable WebM via MediaRecorder for social posts."},"128":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-39","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-3-sales-experience","content":"[ ] **Accessibility & i18n pass**: keyboard navigation for pins, focus states, screen-reader labels, number/currency formatting."},"129":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-40","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **In-app viewer**: RealityKit/SceneKit view of `model.usdz` with the same areas and comments (read `bike-scene/1` JSON), so sales staff can present from the phone offline."},"130":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-41","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **Capture guidance for bikes**: checklist overlay (3 orbits: hub height, saddle height, top-down; close-ups of fork crown, dropouts, rear derailleur, cockpit), shot counter per pass, tips for reflective paint (dulling spray / polarizer), turntable support."},"131":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-42","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **Mac high-detail reconstruction**: `tools/mac-reconstruct` Swift CLI running `PhotogrammetrySession` at `.full` / `.raw` detail from an exported bundle, writing `model.usdz` + `poses.json` back."},"132":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-43","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **On-device GLB export**: convert the USDZ to GLB (ModelIO → glTF writer) so the web viewer never needs conversion."},"133":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-44","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-4-ios-app-depth","content":"[ ] **Upload to viewer**: share sheet target / direct upload of bundles to the web app storage (see Milestone 5)."},"134":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-45","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"[ ] **Catalog page**: list of bikes (cards with turntable thumbnails), search/filter, each opening its scene."},"135":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-46","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"[ ] **Storage**: decide (Cloudflare R2 + Workers, or Supabase) and document; upload bundles, store scenes, auth for editors, public read for shared links."},"136":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-47","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-5-backend--multi-bike-catalog","content":"[ ] **Collaborative comments**: multiple staff editing comments; history."},"137":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-48","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Gaussian splat support**: load `.spz` / splat `.ply` (Scaniverse, Polycam, Luma) via Spark (`@sparkjsdev/spark`) for photoreal paint and chrome; crop box + pins work the same."},"138":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-49","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Performance**: Draco/Meshopt compression, KTX2 textures, lazy loading, 60 fps on iPhone Safari with 50 pins."},"139":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-50","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[x] **E2E tests**: Playwright suite (desktop + iPhone viewport, SwiftShader WebGL) covering view, edit, present, export/import, capture-bundle drop and re-drop, stored captures (reload, Open menu, forget), photo close-ups and lightbox, binary USDC with textures, error toasts, blocked storage, snapshot; synthetic capture-bundle fixtures; unit coverage with ratcheting thresholds; sharded CI job. See docs/TESTING.md."},"140":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-51","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **E2E coverage for app code**: collect V8 coverage from Chromium during the Playwright run (`page.coverage`) and merge it with the unit report, so `ui/app.ts`, `Viewer.ts` and `main.ts` count toward the coverage ratchet."},"141":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-52","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Render on demand**: only render when the camera, model or pins change (idle stage at 0 fps). Saves phone battery and makes the E2E suite much faster on SwiftShader (today every frame costs ~150–250 ms on CPU)."},"142":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-53","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **WebKit E2E project**: run the suite in Playwright WebKit (closest to iPhone Safari) on a macOS runner or with WebKit's Linux deps; the `mobile` project is Chromium with an iPhone viewport today."},"143":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-54","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **One fixture generator**: fold `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` (GLB bundle for the Pages sample) and `tools/fixtures/make-capture.mjs` (USDZ bundle with photo poses) into `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs` as variants, so there is one bike geometry and one pose layout to maintain."},"144":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-55","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **HEIC in E2E**: a small synthetic HEIC photo fixture (needs an encoder at generation time) so the libheif worker path is exercised in Chromium."},"145":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-56","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#milestone-6-quality","content":"[ ] **Docs**: end-to-end guide with screenshots: capture → build → export → annotate → share."},"146":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-57","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"AR \"place the bike in your room\" via Quick Look (`model.usdz` + `<a rel=\"ar\">`)."},"147":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-58","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"Compare two bikes side by side."},"148":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-59","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"Size guide overlay (rider silhouette to scale)."},"149":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-60","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"Measure tool (tap two points → distance in mm)."},"150":{"id":"/docs/roadmap-61","page_id":"/docs/roadmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/roadmap#ideas-parking-lot","content":"_Source: `ROADMAP.md`_"},"151":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"page","content":"How to test","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide"},"152":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-0","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"On your phone (no setup)"},"153":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-1","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-a-laptop","content":"On a laptop"},"154":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-2","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide#make-a-synthetic-capture-bundle","content":"Make a synthetic capture bundle"},"155":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-3","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"What each PR adds"},"156":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-4","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide","content":"A short guide for the owner: how to try what the agents built, on a phone or a laptop. Every\nPR that adds something testable extends the \"What each PR adds\" table at the bottom."},"157":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-5","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"Open the live demo: **https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/**\n(this site lives one level up: https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/)."},"158":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-6","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"The procedural demo bike loads with sample areas and comments."},"159":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-7","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"**View**: drag to orbit, pinch to zoom, tap an area chip (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit…) to fly there."},"160":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-8","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"**Edit**: tap the bike to drop a comment pin; save the current camera as a new area."},"161":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-9","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"**Present**: steps through the areas one by one, as you would with a customer."},"162":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-10","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"The background buttons switch between clear, chroma green, studio and dark."},"163":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-11","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"To try a capture bundle without the iPhone app, download the synthetic one:\n**https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/samples/synthetic-bike.bikecapture.zip**,\nthen in the viewer tap **Open…** and pick it from Files. A red low-poly bike replaces the demo\nand the scene is named \"Synthetic test bike\"."},"164":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-12","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-your-phone-no-setup","content":"The site is redeployed by `tools/publish-pages.sh` after each finished PR, so it shows the\nnewest work in the stack, which may not be merged yet. The footer of the home page says which\ncommit and branch it was built from."},"165":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-13","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-a-laptop","content":"Checks the agents run on every PR (CI runs them too):"},"166":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-14","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#on-a-laptop","content":"How the automated tests work and how to add them: Testing."},"167":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-15","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#make-a-synthetic-capture-bundle","content":"The iPhone app exports `*.bikecapture.zip` (format `bike-capture/1`, see\nArchitecture). To test the import path without a phone:"},"168":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-16","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#make-a-synthetic-capture-bundle","content":"It writes a low-poly bike as `model.glb`, a `manifest.json`, an orbit of camera poses in\n`poses.json` and no photos, all nested in one folder like the real export. Drag the file onto\nthe viewer (or use **Open…**). Dropping the same file again later restores the comments you\nadded to it."},"169":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-17","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#make-a-synthetic-capture-bundle","content":"With a real capture: AirDrop the `.bikecapture.zip` from the iPhone to the laptop and drop it on\nthe viewer. If the model does not show, note what the viewer says and add it to\nManual steps."},"170":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-18","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR            | What to try                                                                           |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #1 Foundation | Demo bike, areas, comments, Edit and Present modes, background switcher, Export JSON. |","table":"table-0"},"171":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-19","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR                       | What to try                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #2 Capture bundle import | **Open…** the synthetic bundle above (or drop it on desktop): it loads and is named from the manifest. Add a comment, reload, open the same file again: the comment is back. |","table":"table-0"},"172":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-20","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR        | What to try                                                                     |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docs site | This site: the home page shows roadmap progress; **Progress** lists every item. |","table":"table-0"},"173":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-21","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #7 Test system | Nothing new to click: `npm run e2e` drives the real viewer through every flow above (demo, edit, present, export/import, capture bundles, stored captures, photo close-ups, error toasts) at desktop and iPhone sizes; `npm run test:coverage` shows unit coverage. The suite found and fixed a bug where a tap right after jumping to an area (with reduced motion on) missed the bike. |","table":"table-0"},"174":{"id":"/docs/testing-guide-22","page_id":"/docs/testing-guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing-guide#what-each-pr-adds","content":"_Source: `docs/TESTING-GUIDE.md`_"},"175":{"id":"/docs/testing","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"page","content":"Testing","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Technical"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing"},"176":{"id":"/docs/testing-0","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"Unit tests"},"177":{"id":"/docs/testing-1","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"What is not unit-tested, and why"},"178":{"id":"/docs/testing-2","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#coverage","content":"Coverage"},"179":{"id":"/docs/testing-3","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"Fixtures"},"180":{"id":"/docs/testing-4","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"`make-capture-bundle.mjs`"},"181":{"id":"/docs/testing-5","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#rendered-photo-bundle","content":"Rendered-photo bundle"},"182":{"id":"/docs/testing-6","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#end-to-end-tests","content":"End-to-end tests"},"183":{"id":"/docs/testing-7","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"The `window.__bike` test hook"},"184":{"id":"/docs/testing-8","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Writing reliable E2E tests"},"185":{"id":"/docs/testing-9","page_id":"/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"What the suite covers"},"186":{"id":"/docs/testing-10","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"Three layers, cheapest first. CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs all of them on every PR."},"187":{"id":"/docs/testing-11","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"| Layer | Where                     | Runs in                                        | Command    |\n| ----- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| Unit  | `apps/web/test/*.test.ts` | Vitest, Node (happy-dom per file where needed) | `npm test` |","table":"table-0"},"188":{"id":"/docs/testing-12","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"| Layer    | Where                   | Runs in | Command                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----------------------- |\n| Coverage | same tests, V8 coverage | Vitest  | `npm run test:coverage` |","table":"table-0"},"189":{"id":"/docs/testing-13","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"| Layer      | Where                    | Runs in                                  | Command       |\n| ---------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| End-to-end | `apps/web/e2e/*.spec.ts` | Playwright, Chromium + SwiftShader WebGL | `npm run e2e` |","table":"table-0"},"190":{"id":"/docs/testing-14","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing","content":"Fixtures for both come from one generator: `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`."},"191":{"id":"/docs/testing-15","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"Pure logic lives in `apps/web/src/scene/` (scene format, store, camera math, capture bundles,\nUI helpers in `helpers.ts`) and is tested in plain Node. When UI code grows a decision (a\ndefault, a message, a URL rule), move it into `src/scene/helpers.ts` and test it there."},"192":{"id":"/docs/testing-16","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"three.js code that needs no WebGL (loaders, `centerOnGround`, the demo bike's geometry) is\ntested in Node too (`viewer-node.test.ts`). three's `FileLoader` needs a `ProgressEvent`\nstub in Node; the test file installs one. Models are passed as `data:` URLs."},"193":{"id":"/docs/testing-17","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"DOM code (`ui/dom.ts`, `viewer/pins.ts`, `ui/photoViewer.ts`, `ui/photoLibrary.ts`,\n`ui/photoDecode.ts`) opts into happy-dom with a first-line comment\n`// @vitest-environment happy-dom`. Browser APIs happy-dom lacks are stubbed per test:\n`createImageBitmap`, `<img>.decode`, `OffscreenCanvas`, `Worker` (photoDecode), pointer capture\n(lightbox gestures), a fake `Viewer` (pins). Decoding itself is mocked in `photoLibrary.test.ts`."},"194":{"id":"/docs/testing-18","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"Storage: `storage/backends.ts` runs against `fake-indexeddb` and a small in-memory OPFS\n(`FakeDir` in `backends.test.ts`); `navigator` is replaced with `vi.stubGlobal`."},"195":{"id":"/docs/testing-19","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"Zip parsing: `zipIndex.test.ts` hand-builds zips byte by byte (zip64 records and extra fields,\nforeign extras, odd methods, lying sizes), branches fflate never writes."},"196":{"id":"/docs/testing-20","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#unit-tests","content":"USD: `usdz.test.ts` loads the committed binary USDC fixtures (`apps/web/test/fixtures/`, made\nby `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py` with Pixar USD); `usd-units.test.ts` drives the crate\ndecoders and composer fast paths directly for encodings the fixtures do not contain."},"197":{"id":"/docs/testing-21","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"Excluded from coverage in `apps/web/vite.config.ts`, each covered by the E2E suite instead:"},"198":{"id":"/docs/testing-22","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File          | Why it cannot run in Node                |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `src/main.ts` | page bootstrap: the whole DOM plus WebGL |","table":"table-1"},"199":{"id":"/docs/testing-23","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File            | Why it cannot run in Node                |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `src/ui/app.ts` | UI controller driving the WebGL `Viewer` |","table":"table-1"},"200":{"id":"/docs/testing-24","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File                   | Why it cannot run in Node                          |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/viewer/Viewer.ts` | `WebGLRenderer`, `OrbitControls`, `ResizeObserver` |","table":"table-1"},"201":{"id":"/docs/testing-25","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File                    | Why it cannot run in Node         |\n| ----------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `src/ui/heic.worker.ts` | a Web Worker running libheif WASM |","table":"table-1"},"202":{"id":"/docs/testing-26","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-is-not-unit-tested-and-why","content":"| File            | Why it cannot run in Node |\n| --------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `src/**/*.d.ts` | type declarations only    |","table":"table-1"},"203":{"id":"/docs/testing-27","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#coverage","content":"`npm run test:coverage` writes `coverage/` (text summary, HTML report, `coverage-summary.json`).\nThresholds in `apps/web/vite.config.ts` are a ratchet set just under the current numbers,\nglobally and for `src/scene/**`; CI fails when coverage drops below them (and the web job\nprints the totals in its step summary). At the time of writing: lines 99.8%, statements 98.9%,\nfunctions 98%, branches 92.8%. When you raise\ncoverage, raise the thresholds in the same PR. Never lower them to make a PR pass."},"204":{"id":"/docs/testing-28","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"Four generators, each with a job. All output is synthetic; no real capture is ever committed."},"205":{"id":"/docs/testing-29","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"| Generator                                | Output                                                              | Used by                                                                           |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs` | the bundle variants below (USDZ, GLB, flat, broken…), deterministic | E2E (global setup), `fixtures.test.ts`, `viewer-node.test.ts`, `npm run fixtures` |","table":"table-2"},"206":{"id":"/docs/testing-30","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"| Generator                                                 | Output                                                                                                          | Used by                                                                                                            |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-capture.mjs` (+ `render-photos.mjs`) | a USDZ bundle off-origin like a real reconstruction, orbit + close-up poses, placeholder or **rendered** photos | `photos.test.ts`, `capture.test.ts`, E2E photo close-ups (`bike-photos.bikecapture.zip`), `npm run fixture:photos` |","table":"table-2"},"207":{"id":"/docs/testing-31","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"| Generator                     | Output                                                                       | Used by                                                                         |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py` | binary USDC (crate) packages in `apps/web/test/fixtures/` (committed, small) | `usdz.test.ts`, E2E \"binary USDC loads textured\"; needs Pixar USD to regenerate |","table":"table-2"},"208":{"id":"/docs/testing-32","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"| Generator                    | Output                           | Used by                                                                 |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` | GLB bundle \"Synthetic test bike\" | the sample on the Pages site (`tools/publish-pages.sh`), manual testing |","table":"table-2"},"209":{"id":"/docs/testing-33","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#fixtures","content":"Folding the three JS generators into one is a ROADMAP follow-up."},"210":{"id":"/docs/testing-34","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"`buildFixtures()` returns every fixture as bytes and is also imported by unit tests. Output is\nbyte-for-byte deterministic (fixed zip timestamps, rounded floats), so nothing binary is\ncommitted. What it makes:"},"211":{"id":"/docs/testing-35","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                   | What it exercises                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike.bikecapture.zip` | iOS layout (everything under one folder): manifest, ASCII-USD `model.usdz` of a low-poly vertex-colored bike (wheels, frame tubes, fork, cockpit, saddle, drivetrain as named meshes), `poses.json` with 32 cameras on three rings looking at the bike, 32 tiny placeholder PNG photos, `record.json` |","table":"table-3"},"212":{"id":"/docs/testing-36","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                       | What it exercises                                                |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike-glb.bikecapture.zip` | same bike as GLB (three's `GLTFExporter` in Node, vertex colors) |","table":"table-3"},"213":{"id":"/docs/testing-37","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                        | What it exercises                    |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `bike-flat.bikecapture.zip` | flat zip with Finder `__MACOSX` junk |","table":"table-3"},"214":{"id":"/docs/testing-38","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                                | What it exercises                          |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `bike-broken-poses.bikecapture.zip` | invalid `poses.json`: opens with a warning |","table":"table-3"},"215":{"id":"/docs/testing-39","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                            | What it exercises                  |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `bike-no-model.bikecapture.zip` | capture never reconstructed: error |","table":"table-3"},"216":{"id":"/docs/testing-40","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                        | What it exercises              |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `not-a-zip.bikecapture.zip` | text with a `.zip` name: error |","table":"table-3"},"217":{"id":"/docs/testing-41","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"| File                    | What it exercises |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `bike.usdz`, `bike.glb` | bare model files  |","table":"table-3"},"218":{"id":"/docs/testing-42","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#make-capture-bundlemjs","content":"The photos are PNG stand-ins: real captures have HEIC, which Node cannot encode."},"219":{"id":"/docs/testing-43","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#rendered-photo-bundle","content":"The E2E global setup (`apps/web/e2e/global-setup.ts`) also renders the `make-capture.mjs` bike\nfrom each of its poses with `render-photos.mjs` (headless Chromium, three.js, the iPhone wide\ncamera's field of view) and writes `bike-photos.bikecapture.zip`, so photo close-ups are ranked\nand shown from real images of the fixture."},"220":{"id":"/docs/testing-44","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#end-to-end-tests","content":"Playwright drives the **production build** (`vite build` + `vite preview` on port 4190, started\nby the config's `webServer`) in two projects: `desktop` (1280×800, every spec) and `mobile`\n(iPhone 14 viewport with touch, DPR 1 to keep CPU rendering fast; only the specs where layout and\ntouch matter: view, edit, present, photos). WebGL runs on SwiftShader\n(`--use-angle=swiftshader --enable-unsafe-swiftshader`), so no GPU is needed. CI splits the\nsuite into two parallel shards (`--shard=1/2`, `2/2`)."},"221":{"id":"/docs/testing-45","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#end-to-end-tests","content":"Browser: CI runs `npx playwright install --with-deps --only-shell chromium`. On a machine with a\npreinstalled Chromium (e.g. the agent containers: `/opt/pw-browsers/chromium`), do not run\n`playwright install`; set `PW_CHROMIUM_PATH=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium` and the config uses it as\n`launchOptions.executablePath`. `@playwright/test` is pinned to the version whose browsers are\npreinstalled there."},"222":{"id":"/docs/testing-46","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"`main.ts` exposes `window.__bike = { app, store, viewer, ready }` only in the dev server or when\nthe URL has `?e2e` (the suite always adds it). Tests use it to:"},"223":{"id":"/docs/testing-47","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"wait for state instead of sleeping: `ready` (boot finished), a model in `viewer.modelRoot`,\n`viewer.flying` (camera animation running);"},"224":{"id":"/docs/testing-48","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"find a point on the model to tap: `modelPoint()` in `e2e/helpers.ts` asks the app's own\n`viewer.pick()` and checks `document.elementFromPoint` so the tap lands on the canvas, not a pin;"},"225":{"id":"/docs/testing-49","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"read the scene for assertions (`store.scene`)."},"226":{"id":"/docs/testing-50","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#the-window__bike-test-hook","content":"Everything else goes through the real UI: clicks, taps, keys, the file picker\n(`setInputFiles`), real `DragEvent` drops with a `DataTransfer`, dialogs and downloads. Keep the\nhook read-mostly; if a test needs to mutate app state through it, that is a sign a UI path is\nmissing."},"227":{"id":"/docs/testing-51","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Never `waitForTimeout`. Wait on app state (`waitForFunction`, `expect.poll`) or on web-first\nassertions (`toHaveText`, `toHaveCount`, `toHaveAttribute`)."},"228":{"id":"/docs/testing-52","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Camera flights are instant because the suite emulates `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, which\nthe viewer honors; a test that wants the animation calls\n`page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion: 'no-preference' })` and waits for `viewer.flying === false`."},"229":{"id":"/docs/testing-53","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Use `collectErrors(page)` and assert it is empty where a flow should be clean."},"230":{"id":"/docs/testing-54","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Screenshots are for humans: `snap(page, testInfo, name)` saves to `test-results/` and attaches\nto the HTML report. Do not add pixel-diff assertions; SwiftShader output differs across\nmachines."},"231":{"id":"/docs/testing-55","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"Tests run in parallel across fresh browser contexts, so each test starts from an empty\n`localStorage` and the seeded demo."},"232":{"id":"/docs/testing-56","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#writing-reliable-e2e-tests","content":"On CI a failing run uploads `playwright-report/` and `test-results/` (traces, screenshots) as\nthe `playwright-report` artifact. CI retries once; a test that only passes on retry is reported\nas flaky and should be fixed, not ignored."},"233":{"id":"/docs/testing-57","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`view.spec.ts`: demo loads with seeded areas/comments/pins and no console errors; fly to an\narea and back; comment focus; background modes (and the chroma-green opaque clear); Snapshot\ndownloads a real PNG; Reset view."},"234":{"id":"/docs/testing-58","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`edit.spec.ts`: add/edit/delete a comment picked on the canvas; persistence across reload;\nCancel/Escape; default area; save/rename/set view/delete areas; bike details."},"235":{"id":"/docs/testing-59","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`present.spec.ts`: keys (←, →, space, Esc) and ‹ › buttons with wrap-around; `?mode=present`."},"236":{"id":"/docs/testing-60","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`files.spec.ts`: export JSON → re-import; `?scene=` published scene (routed); capture bundles\nvia picker and drag-and-drop (USDZ, GLB, flat); re-drop after reload restores comments;\nbroken poses warning; bare model drop; error toasts for seven kinds of bad files."},"237":{"id":"/docs/testing-61","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`storage.spec.ts`: everything still works with `localStorage` throwing."},"238":{"id":"/docs/testing-62","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`capture-cache.spec.ts`: a reload reopens the last capture from OPFS with its comments; the\nOpen menu lists stored captures (most recent first, size, current one marked), switches between\nthem, closes on Esc / outside click, \"Choose a file…\", forgets them; forgotten means a reload\nasks for the zip again. `files.spec.ts` keeps the re-drop flow with capture storage blocked\n(`blockCaptureStorage()`)."},"239":{"id":"/docs/testing-63","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`photos.spec.ts`: a saved area shows its best photos (all thumbnails decode), the lightbox\nsteps with ←/→ and ‹ › with wrap-around, Esc closes only the lightbox; Present mode shows the\nstrip; after a reload the thumbnails come from browser storage."},"240":{"id":"/docs/testing-64","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"`files.spec.ts` also drops the committed binary USDC fixture and checks it renders with its\ndiffuse and normal textures decoded."},"241":{"id":"/docs/testing-65","page_id":"/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/testing#what-the-suite-covers","content":"_Source: `docs/TESTING.md`_"}},"count":241},"sorting":{"language":"english","sortableProperties":["content","page_id","type","url"],"sortablePropertiesWithTypes":{"content":"string","page_id":"string","type":"string","url":"string"},"sorts":{"content":{"docs":{"1":125,"2":237,"3":138,"4":73,"5":132,"6":229,"7":74,"8":185,"9":182,"10":91,"11":149,"12":111,"13":114,"14":113,"15":115,"16":112,"17":161,"18":218,"19":205,"20":71,"21":72,"22":59,"23":51,"24":56,"25":69,"26":178,"27":223,"28":78,"29":77,"30":89,"31":168,"32":202,"33":154,"34":68,"35":63,"36":61,"37":142,"38":120,"39":127,"40":1,"41":134,"42":227,"43":123,"44":146,"45":208,"46":186,"47":133,"48":141,"49":230,"50":131,"51":155,"52":0,"53":157,"54":189,"55":207,"56":194,"57":177,"58":121,"59":52,"60":60,"61":57,"62":67,"63":66,"64":192,"65":85,"66":225,"67":140,"68":191,"69":196,"70":2,"71":184,"72":130,"73":49,"74":50,"75":144,"76":203,"77":6,"78":165,"79":220,"80":54,"81":53,"82":65,"83":64,"84":58,"85":3,"86":190,"87":199,"88":198,"89":169,"90":170,"91":171,"92":172,"93":173,"94":174,"95":175,"96":160,"97":213,"98":166,"99":44,"100":10,"101":32,"102":233,"103":200,"104":126,"105":188,"106":162,"107":136,"108":43,"109":46,"110":13,"111":12,"112":48,"113":40,"114":42,"115":9,"116":18,"117":47,"118":25,"119":39,"120":27,"121":31,"122":34,"123":17,"124":23,"125":36,"126":11,"127":35,"128":8,"129":24,"130":14,"131":26,"132":28,"133":38,"134":15,"135":37,"136":16,"137":21,"138":30,"139":45,"140":20,"141":33,"142":41,"143":29,"144":22,"145":19,"146":124,"147":137,"148":204,"149":167,"150":7,"151":159,"152":181,"153":179,"154":164,"155":234,"156":122,"157":183,"158":217,"159":70,"160":55,"161":62,"162":212,"163":224,"164":219,"165":135,"166":158,"167":215,"168":163,"169":238,"170":118,"171":116,"172":119,"173":117,"174":4,"175":209,"176":226,"177":235,"178":139,"179":151,"180":83,"181":197,"182":145,"183":211,"184":239,"185":236,"186":221,"187":110,"188":109,"189":108,"190":152,"191":193,"192":222,"193":143,"194":206,"195":240,"196":228,"197":148,"198":103,"199":101,"200":100,"201":98,"202":102,"203":84,"204":156,"205":105,"206":104,"207":106,"208":107,"209":153,"210":75,"211":99,"212":96,"213":94,"214":92,"215":93,"216":95,"217":97,"218":216,"219":214,"220":187,"221":128,"222":82,"223":232,"224":150,"225":195,"226":147,"227":176,"228":129,"229":231,"230":201,"231":210,"232":180,"233":90,"234":79,"235":87,"236":81,"237":88,"238":76,"239":86,"240":80,"241":5},"orderedDocs":[[52,"_Source: `CHANGELOG.md`_"],[40,"_Source: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`_"],[70,"_Source: `docs/GOALS.md`_"],[85,"_Source: `docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md`_"],[174,"_Source: `docs/TESTING-GUIDE.md`_"],[241,"_Source: `docs/TESTING.md`_"],[77,"_Source: `README.md`_"],[150,"_Source: `ROADMAP.md`_"],[128,"[ ] **Accessibility & i18n pass**: keyboard navigation for pins, focus states, screen-reader labels, number/currency formatting."],[115,"[ ] **Auto-orient captures**: detect the ground plane / longest horizontal axis so a scanned bike stands upright facing +X; expose rotate/scale/offset controls in Edit mode (writes `model.rotation/scale/offset`)."],[100,"[ ] **Auto-publish on develop**: a workflow (`contents: write`) that runs `tools/publish-pages.sh --source develop` on every push to `develop`, so the site stays current even when no agent session runs."],[126,"[ ] **Branding**: shop logo, accent color and font in scene settings; applied to Present mode."],[111,"[ ] **Cache large models without a main-thread copy**: write models to OPFS from a worker (`createSyncAccessHandle`) or straight from the dropped `File` stream, so a 300 MB capture does not briefly double memory on phones."],[110,"[ ] **Capture cache on real Safari / iOS**: verify OPFS `createWritable()` vs. the IndexedDB fallback, quota numbers and `persist()` behavior on iPhone Safari and a home-screen web app; tune the 500 MB budget for phones."],[130,"[ ] **Capture guidance for bikes**: checklist overlay (3 orbits: hub height, saddle height, top-down; close-ups of fork crown, dropouts, rear derailleur, cockpit), shot counter per pass, tips for reflective paint (dulling spray / polarizer), turntable support."],[134,"[ ] **Catalog page**: list of bikes (cards with turntable thumbnails), search/filter, each opening its scene."],[136,"[ ] **Collaborative comments**: multiple staff editing comments; history."],[123,"[ ] **Comment polish**: leader lines from pin to card in Present mode, auto-advance/kiosk mode, comment ordering (drag to reorder), markdown-lite (bold, bullet lists) in bodies."],[116,"[ ] **Crop box for area-mode / splat captures**: draggable box in Edit mode that clips everything outside (clipping planes), saved in the scene, so area-mode scans get a clean background."],[145,"[ ] **Docs**: end-to-end guide with screenshots: capture → build → export → annotate → share."],[140,"[ ] **E2E coverage for app code**: collect V8 coverage from Chromium during the Playwright run (`page.coverage`) and merge it with the unit report, so `ui/app.ts`, `Viewer.ts` and `main.ts` count toward the coverage ratchet."],[137,"[ ] **Gaussian splat support**: load `.spz` / splat `.ply` (Scaniverse, Polycam, Luma) via Spark (`@sparkjsdev/spark`) for photoreal paint and chrome; crop box + pins work the same."],[144,"[ ] **HEIC in E2E**: a small synthetic HEIC photo fixture (needs an encoder at generation time) so the libheif worker path is exercised in Chromium."],[124,"[ ] **Hotspot auto-suggest**: for captures, propose default areas (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit, Wheels, Saddle) by letting the user tap each part once; camera view computed from tapped point + local bounds."],[129,"[ ] **In-app viewer**: RealityKit/SceneKit view of `model.usdz` with the same areas and comments (read `bike-scene/1` JSON), so sales staff can present from the phone offline."],[118,"[ ] **iOS JPEG photo export**: write `images/*.jpg` (or a `photos/` folder of 2048 px JPEGs) next to the HEICs in the bundle so Chrome/Firefox skip the 2 MB WASM HEIC decoder and decoding is instant; the web side already prefers whatever decodes natively."],[131,"[ ] **Mac high-detail reconstruction**: `tools/mac-reconstruct` Swift CLI running `PhotogrammetrySession` at `.full` / `.raw` detail from an exported bundle, writing `model.usdz` + `poses.json` back."],[120,"[ ] **Occlusion-aware close-ups**: raycast from each candidate camera to the target against the loaded mesh and drop photos where the bike hides it."],[132,"[ ] **On-device GLB export**: convert the USDZ to GLB (ModelIO → glTF writer) so the web viewer never needs conversion."],[143,"[ ] **One fixture generator**: fold `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` (GLB bundle for the Pages sample) and `tools/fixtures/make-capture.mjs` (USDZ bundle with photo poses) into `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs` as variants, so there is one bike geometry and one pose layout to maintain."],[138,"[ ] **Performance**: Draco/Meshopt compression, KTX2 textures, lazy loading, 60 fps on iPhone Safari with 50 pins."],[121,"[ ] **Pin favourite close-ups**: let staff star photos for an area (the schema already has `Hotspot.photos`) and show starred ones first, also in shared links."],[101,"[ ] **PR previews**: publish each open stack PR under `/bike-3d-brew/pr/<n>/` (docs + viewer) and link them from the Progress page, so the owner can test a PR before merging it."],[141,"[ ] **Render on demand**: only render when the camera, model or pins change (idle stage at 0 fps). Saves phone battery and makes the E2E suite much faster on SwiftShader (today every frame costs ~150–250 ms on CPU)."],[122,"[ ] **Shareable read-only link**: `?scene=` URL loads a published scene in Present mode with editing hidden; \"Copy share link\" button. Scenes + models served from `apps/web/public/scenes/<id>/`."],[127,"[ ] **Snapshot / video export**: high-res PNG with transparent or green background; 360° turntable WebM via MediaRecorder for social posts."],[125,"[ ] **Spec sheet**: per-bike key specs table (frame material, groupset, weight, sizes) shown in Present mode intro and exported."],[135,"[ ] **Storage**: decide (Cloudflare R2 + Workers, or Supabase) and document; upload bundles, store scenes, auth for editors, public read for shared links."],[133,"[ ] **Upload to viewer**: share sheet target / direct upload of bundles to the web app storage (see Milestone 5)."],[119,"[ ] **Validate close-ups on a real capture**: confirm Object Capture poses share the USDZ frame and the 65° landscape intrinsics assumption (portrait captures, EXIF rotation); read real intrinsics if the iOS app can export them."],[113,"[ ] **Verify a real Object Capture USDZ**: load a real `model.usdz` (owner's iPhone, see docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md), compare against Quick Look; turn anything off into a fixture-based test (synthetic re-creation, never the capture itself)."],[142,"[ ] **WebKit E2E project**: run the suite in Playwright WebKit (closest to iPhone Safari) on a macOS runner or with WebKit's Linux deps; the `mobile` project is Chromium with an iPhone viewport today."],[114,"[ ] **Weld USDZ meshes**: three expands face-varying meshes to 3 vertices per triangle (~3M vertices for a 1M-triangle capture); merge identical corners into an indexed geometry to cut GPU memory, and consider decimating for phones."],[108,"[x] **Capture bundle import**: drop `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer, unzip in the browser (fflate), load `model.usdz`, read `manifest.json` and `poses.json`, name the scene from the manifest. Unit-test the bundle parser with a synthetic zip."],[99,"[x] **Docs & progress site**: Fumadocs static site (`apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown, with a roadmap progress dashboard and a \"How to test\" guide, published with the viewer to GitHub Pages by `tools/publish-pages.sh` (site at `/bike-3d-brew/`, viewer at `/bike-3d-brew/app/`)."],[139,"[x] **E2E tests**: Playwright suite (desktop + iPhone viewport, SwiftShader WebGL) covering view, edit, present, export/import, capture-bundle drop and re-drop, stored captures (reload, Open menu, forget), photo close-ups and lightbox, binary USDC with textures, error toasts, blocked storage, snapshot; synthetic capture-bundle fixtures; unit coverage with ratcheting thresholds; sharded CI job. See docs/TESTING.md."],[109,"[x] **Keep captures across reloads**: cache the unzipped model of the last opened bundles in IndexedDB/OPFS (best effort, quota-aware) so a reload reopens a capture scene without re-dropping the `.bikecapture.zip`."],[117,"[x] **Photo close-ups per area**: use `poses.json` to find the capture photos that look most directly at each area target (angle + distance score) and show them as a filmstrip under the area; tap to open full screen. HEIC → JPEG conversion at export time on iOS if browsers can't decode HEIC."],[112,"[x] **USDZ robustness**: three r186 reads binary USDC; `apps/web/src/viewer/usd/` fixes its inline-value decoding, speeds up large meshes ~10×, waits for packed textures and falls back to a `tools/usdz-to-glb.py` hint. Synthetic Object-Capture-like fixtures from `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`."],[73,"**`apps/ios`**: iPhone capture app (Apple Object Capture: background removed automatically, on-device 3D build, camera poses, shareable bundle)."],[74,"**`apps/web`**: three.js viewer and editor: clear / chroma-green / studio backgrounds, fly-to areas, comment pins, presentation mode, JSON export."],[23,"**Budget**: LRU by last use, `min(500 MB, 50% of the quota − other usage)` from\n`navigator.storage.estimate()`. A bundle larger than the whole budget is simply not cached."],[59,"**Capture → viewer in under 15 minutes** with no desktop software: capture on iPhone,\nAirDrop the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer."],[81,"**Close-ups on a real capture**: open a real `.bikecapture.zip` with a few areas and check that\neach area's first photos really show it, in Chrome (WASM HEIC path) and iPhone Safari (native)."],[80,"**Decide on the HEIC decoder license**: photo close-ups decode HEIC in Chrome/Firefox with\n`libheif-js` (LGPL-3.0), shipped as a separate, lazily loaded worker chunk. Fine for a private\ntool; before a public release, either confirm LGPL compliance (unmodified library in its own\nfile, notice in the about/credits) or remove it once the iOS app exports JPEGs (see ROADMAP)."],[160,"**Edit**: tap the bike to drop a comment pin; save the current camera as a new area."],[24,"**Failure**: every call is best effort. Any storage error leaves the app as if the cache did\nnot exist; entries whose files vanished (browser eviction) are dropped from the index."],[61,"**Fast on phones**: first model visible in < 3 s on iPhone Safari over 4G for a 20 MB model;\n60 fps orbiting with 50 pins."],[84,"**GitHub Pages**: done by the owner on 2026-10-27 (Settings → Pages → Deploy from branch\n`gh-pages`). The site is published from this repo by `tools/publish-pages.sh`."],[22,"**Keys**: one entry per `bundle:` model URL; files live under `cap-<slug>-<fnv1a(url)>/…` and an\n`index.json` lists entries (validated on read). An entry remembers the scene id it was opened\nas, so a different bike exported with the same zip filename never loads the wrong model."],[60,"**Looks like the real bike**: textures, thin parts (spokes, cables) acceptable; background gone."],[36,"**Photos** (`src/ui/photoLibrary.ts`): extracted one at a time from the dropped zip via its\ncentral directory (`src/scene/zipIndex.ts`: the `File` stays on disk, nothing else is inflated),\ndecoded natively (`createImageBitmap`, then `<img>`; Safari reads HEIC), else HEIC goes to a\nmodule worker that lazily loads libheif (`libheif-js`, WASM, ~2 MB, LGPL-3.0, only fetched when a\nHEIC photo is shown). Results are downscaled to JPEG (360 px thumbnails, 2048 px full) and added\nto the capture cache entry, so after a reload the photos already seen still show without the zip."],[161,"**Present**: steps through the areas one by one, as you would with a customer."],[35,"**Ranking** (`src/scene/photos.ts`, pure): keep photos whose frustum contains the target\n(assumed iPhone wide camera, 65° × 51°, landscape sensor; poses carry no intrinsics), drop\ncameras behind the surface (`side` hint), score `0.45·centered + 0.35·closeness + 0.2·facing`\n(closeness relative to the nearest usable photo, so units do not matter), and skip near-duplicate\nviewpoints. Occlusion is not tested."],[83,"**Real iPhone capture test** (needs an iPhone with LiDAR, iOS 18+): build `apps/ios`, capture a\nbike, export the `.bikecapture.zip`, drop it on the viewer. Report whether the USDZ loads."],[82,"**Real Object Capture USDZ in the viewer** (needs a real capture): drop the `model.usdz` (or\nthe `.bikecapture.zip`) on the viewer and compare with Quick Look on the Mac/iPhone: textures\npresent and not flipped, size in meters, bike upright, normal-map bumps not exaggerated. The\nbrowser console logs `USDZ …: N triangles, unzip/parse/build ms`; note those numbers in the\nPR. If anything is off, describe the file structure (`usdcat model.usdz | head -80` without\nsharing the capture) so an agent can re-create it in `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`."],[63,"**Robust**: untrusted files never crash the app; every failure says what to do next."],[62,"**Selling tool, not a 3D toy**: areas and comments are the primary UI; present mode is\nusable by a non-technical salesperson with one hand."],[34,"**Spaces.** A pose is a column-major camera→reconstruction matrix, camera looking down -Z,\n+Y up. Scene positions are in model-root space. `Viewer.setModel` adds `centerOnGround(object)`\nto the model root, so `modelRoot ⟵ reconstruction` is the loaded object's local matrix (the\ncentering shift plus any root transform the loader applied) times the identity wrapper:\n`src/viewer/captureSpace.ts`. The scene's `model.rotation/scale/offset` sit on the model root\nitself and never enter the mapping. A unit test runs the fixture USDZ through three's\n`USDLoader` + `centerOnGround` and checks the expected close-ups win."],[25,"**UI**: \"Open…\" becomes a small menu once something is stored: \"Choose a file…\" plus the stored\ncaptures (name, size, × to forget)."],[159,"**View**: drag to orbit, pinch to zoom, tap an area chip (Fork, Drivetrain, Cockpit…) to fly there."],[20,"**What**: the model bytes, `manifest.json`, `poses.json` and the image list. Lazily extracted\nfiles (photos, thumbnails) can be added to an entry later (`putFile`) and are evicted with it.\nThe zip itself is not kept (HEIC photos make it hundreds of MB)."],[21,"**Where**: OPFS (`navigator.storage.getDirectory()`, folder `bike-captures/`, flat\npercent-encoded file names), falling back to IndexedDB (`bike-3d-brew` / `files`) when OPFS is\nmissing, has no `createWritable()` (older Safari) or refuses a probe write. Neither → no cache,\nthe old \"drop the zip again\" behavior. `navigator.storage.persist()` is requested once per page\nload, on the first store."],[4,"`bike-capture/1` (iOS export zip)"],[7,"`bike-scene/1` (viewer JSON, `*.bike.json`)"],[210,"`buildFixtures()` returns every fixture as bytes and is also imported by unit tests. Output is\nbyte-for-byte deterministic (fixed zip timestamps, rounded floats), so nothing binary is\ncommitted. What it makes:"],[238,"`capture-cache.spec.ts`: a reload reopens the last capture from OPFS with its comments; the\nOpen menu lists stored captures (most recent first, size, current one marked), switches between\nthem, closes on Esc / outside click, \"Choose a file…\", forgets them; forgotten means a reload\nasks for the zip again. `files.spec.ts` keeps the re-drop flow with capture storage blocked\n(`blockCaptureStorage()`)."],[29,"`composer.ts` (`FastUSDComposer`): typed-array fast path for all-triangle meshes. Stock three took\n~1.4–2.2 s to build a 1M-triangle mesh (JS arrays per index); this takes ~0.2 s, same output."],[28,"`crate.ts` (`CrateParser`): values the crate stores **inline** that r186 misreads: small integral\n`double2/3/4` and `half3/4` (packed int8, e.g. `xformOp:translate = (0, 0, 5)` became a number and\ncrashed the transform), negative `int`, `half`; plus scalar `half3/4`, `quath`, `int4`, `matrix2d/3d`."],[234,"`edit.spec.ts`: add/edit/delete a comment picked on the canvas; persistence across reload;\nCancel/Escape; default area; save/rename/set view/delete areas; bike details."],[240,"`files.spec.ts` also drops the committed binary USDC fixture and checks it renders with its\ndiffuse and normal textures decoded."],[236,"`files.spec.ts`: export JSON → re-import; `?scene=` published scene (routed); capture bundles\nvia picker and drag-and-drop (USDZ, GLB, flat); re-drop after reload restores comments;\nbroken poses warning; bare model drop; error toasts for seven kinds of bad files."],[222,"`main.ts` exposes `window.__bike = { app, store, viewer, ready }` only in the dev server or when\nthe URL has `?e2e` (the suite always adds it). Tests use it to:"],[180,"`make-capture-bundle.mjs`"],[203,"`npm run test:coverage` writes `coverage/` (text summary, HTML report, `coverage-summary.json`).\nThresholds in `apps/web/vite.config.ts` are a ratchet set just under the current numbers,\nglobally and for `src/scene/**`; CI fails when coverage drops below them (and the web job\nprints the totals in its step summary). At the time of writing: lines 99.8%, statements 98.9%,\nfunctions 98%, branches 92.8%. When you raise\ncoverage, raise the thresholds in the same PR. Never lower them to make a PR pass."],[65,"`npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build` and the E2E suite pass; CI green."],[239,"`photos.spec.ts`: a saved area shows its best photos (all thumbnails decode), the lightbox\nsteps with ←/→ and ‹ › with wrap-around, Esc closes only the lightbox; Present mode shows the\nstrip; after a reload the thumbnails come from browser storage."],[235,"`present.spec.ts`: keys (←, →, space, Esc) and ‹ › buttons with wrap-around; `?mode=present`."],[237,"`storage.spec.ts`: everything still works with `localStorage` throwing."],[30,"`usdz.ts` (`loadUsd`): unzips only USD layers and images, takes the first layer as root (falls back\nto the first USD layer anywhere), composes, waits for textures (blob URLs created and revoked by\nthree per image), halves three's normal-map strength for the standard scale 2 / bias -1 decode,\nand reports undecodable textures as warnings instead of failing."],[233,"`view.spec.ts`: demo loads with seeded areas/comments/pins and no console errors; fly to an\narea and back; comment focus; background modes (and the chroma-green opaque clear); Snapshot\ndownloads a real PNG; Reset view."],[10,"`wesbos/3d-model-anything` records RoomPlan + LiDAR mesh + posed photos, then an AI agent\nrebuilds the room in three.js. A bike is one object with thin tubes, spokes and cables, so we\nuse Apple's Object Capture: guided orbits, **automatic object masking** (the background is\nremoved during reconstruction; no green screen needed) and a textured USDZ. We keep Wes's\nkey idea of **posed photos**: `poses.json` tells us where each photo was taken, so the viewer\ncan show real close-up photos for an area (e.g. the fork crown) next to the 3D view."],[214,"| File                                | What it exercises                          |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `bike-broken-poses.bikecapture.zip` | invalid `poses.json`: opens with a warning |"],[215,"| File                            | What it exercises                  |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `bike-no-model.bikecapture.zip` | capture never reconstructed: error |"],[213,"| File                        | What it exercises                    |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `bike-flat.bikecapture.zip` | flat zip with Finder `__MACOSX` junk |"],[216,"| File                        | What it exercises              |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `not-a-zip.bikecapture.zip` | text with a `.zip` name: error |"],[212,"| File                       | What it exercises                                                |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike-glb.bikecapture.zip` | same bike as GLB (three's `GLTFExporter` in Node, vertex colors) |"],[217,"| File                    | What it exercises |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `bike.usdz`, `bike.glb` | bare model files  |"],[201,"| File                    | Why it cannot run in Node         |\n| ----------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `src/ui/heic.worker.ts` | a Web Worker running libheif WASM |"],[211,"| File                   | What it exercises                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bike.bikecapture.zip` | iOS layout (everything under one folder): manifest, ASCII-USD `model.usdz` of a low-poly vertex-colored bike (wheels, frame tubes, fork, cockpit, saddle, drivetrain as named meshes), `poses.json` with 32 cameras on three rings looking at the bike, 32 tiny placeholder PNG photos, `record.json` |"],[200,"| File                   | Why it cannot run in Node                          |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `src/viewer/Viewer.ts` | `WebGLRenderer`, `OrbitControls`, `ResizeObserver` |"],[199,"| File            | Why it cannot run in Node                |\n| --------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `src/ui/app.ts` | UI controller driving the WebGL `Viewer` |"],[202,"| File            | Why it cannot run in Node |\n| --------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `src/**/*.d.ts` | type declarations only    |"],[198,"| File          | Why it cannot run in Node                |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `src/main.ts` | page bootstrap: the whole DOM plus WebGL |"],[206,"| Generator                                                 | Output                                                                                                          | Used by                                                                                                            |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-capture.mjs` (+ `render-photos.mjs`) | a USDZ bundle off-origin like a real reconstruction, orbit + close-up poses, placeholder or **rendered** photos | `photos.test.ts`, `capture.test.ts`, E2E photo close-ups (`bike-photos.bikecapture.zip`), `npm run fixture:photos` |"],[205,"| Generator                                | Output                                                              | Used by                                                                           |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs` | the bundle variants below (USDZ, GLB, flat, broken…), deterministic | E2E (global setup), `fixtures.test.ts`, `viewer-node.test.ts`, `npm run fixtures` |"],[207,"| Generator                     | Output                                                                       | Used by                                                                         |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py` | binary USDC (crate) packages in `apps/web/test/fixtures/` (committed, small) | `usdz.test.ts`, E2E \"binary USDC loads textured\"; needs Pixar USD to regenerate |"],[208,"| Generator                    | Output                           | Used by                                                                 |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` | GLB bundle \"Synthetic test bike\" | the sample on the Pages site (`tools/publish-pages.sh`), manual testing |"],[189,"| Layer      | Where                    | Runs in                                  | Command       |\n| ---------- | ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| End-to-end | `apps/web/e2e/*.spec.ts` | Playwright, Chromium + SwiftShader WebGL | `npm run e2e` |"],[188,"| Layer    | Where                   | Runs in | Command                 |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | ------- | ----------------------- |\n| Coverage | same tests, V8 coverage | Vitest  | `npm run test:coverage` |"],[187,"| Layer | Where                     | Runs in                                        | Command    |\n| ----- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ---------- |\n| Unit  | `apps/web/test/*.test.ts` | Vitest, Node (happy-dom per file where needed) | `npm test` |"],[12,"| Path            | Content                                                                                                        |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `manifest.json` | `{ schema, name, createdAt, device, systemVersion, mode: \"object\"\\|\"area\", model, poses, images, imageCount }` |"],[16,"| Path          | Content             |\n| ------------- | ------------------- |\n| `record.json` | app-internal record |"],[14,"| Path         | Content                                                                                              |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `poses.json` | `{ schema: \"bike-poses/1\", samples: [{ sample, file, transform[16] }] }` (column-major camera→model) |"],[13,"| Path         | Content                       |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| `model.usdz` | reconstruction, meters, +Y up |"],[15,"| Path      | Content                    |\n| --------- | -------------------------- |\n| `images/` | Object Capture HEIC photos |"],[171,"| PR                       | What to try                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #2 Capture bundle import | **Open…** the synthetic bundle above (or drop it on desktop): it loads and is named from the manifest. Add a comment, reload, open the same file again: the comment is back. |"],[173,"| PR             | What to try                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #7 Test system | Nothing new to click: `npm run e2e` drives the real viewer through every flow above (demo, edit, present, export/import, capture bundles, stored captures, photo close-ups, error toasts) at desktop and iPhone sizes; `npm run test:coverage` shows unit coverage. The suite found and fixed a bug where a tap right after jumping to an area (with reduced motion on) missed the bike. |"],[170,"| PR            | What to try                                                                           |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #1 Foundation | Demo bike, areas, comments, Edit and Present modes, background switcher, Export JSON. |"],[172,"| PR        | What to try                                                                     |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docs site | This site: the home page shows roadmap progress; **Progress** lists every item. |"],[38,"~~Does three.js read Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC)?~~ Yes, with the fixes above, verified on\nsynthetic Object-Capture-like files. Still to confirm on a real capture (docs/MANUAL-STEPS.md)."],[58,"A bike shop captures a bike with an iPhone in a few minutes and gets a background-free,\nphotoreal 3D model that sales staff (in store, on a tablet) and customers (on a shared link)\ncan spin, zoom into named areas (fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and read pinned sales comments."],[156,"A short guide for the owner: how to try what the agents built, on a phone or a laptop. Every\nPR that adds something testable extends the \"What each PR adds\" table at the bottom."],[43,"Added"],[146,"AR \"place the bike in your room\" via Quick Look (`model.usdz` + `<a rel=\"ar\">`)."],[1,"Architecture"],[104,"Areas (hotspots) and sales comments pinned to the model surface, edit + present modes"],[39,"Bike size vs. Object Capture's bounding box limits: area mode is the fallback."],[221,"Browser: CI runs `npx playwright install --with-deps --only-shell chromium`. On a machine with a\npreinstalled Chromium (e.g. the agent containers: `/opt/pw-browsers/chromium`), do not run\n`playwright install`; set `PW_CHROMIUM_PATH=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium` and the config uses it as\n`launchOptions.executablePath`. `@playwright/test` is pinned to the version whose browsers are\npreinstalled there."],[228,"Camera flights are instant because the suite emulates `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, which\nthe viewer honors; a test that wants the animation calls\n`page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion: 'no-preference' })` and waits for `viewer.flying === false`."],[72,"Capture bikes with an iPhone, show them as background-free 3D models, zoom into components\n(fork, drivetrain, cockpit…) and pin sales comments on them."],[50,"Capture bundle import: drop an iPhone `*.bikecapture.zip` on the viewer; it is unzipped in the browser, the model loads and the scene is named from the manifest. Re-dropping a bundle restores its comments. (#2)"],[5,"Capture cache (browser storage)"],[47,"Captures survive reloads: opened `*.bikecapture.zip` bundles are kept in browser storage (OPFS, IndexedDB fallback, LRU under a quota-aware budget) and reopen automatically; \"Open…\" lists stored captures with size and a forget button. Synthetic fixture generator in `tools/fixtures/`. (#5)"],[41,"Changelog"],[165,"Checks the agents run on every PR (CI runs them too):"],[107,"CI: web typecheck/test/build, unsigned iOS build on macOS, Pages deploy workflow"],[147,"Compare two bikes side by side."],[3,"Contracts"],[178,"Coverage"],[67,"Docs (ROADMAP, CHANGELOG, ARCHITECTURE, guides) updated in the same PR."],[48,"Docs & progress site (Fumadocs, `apps/docs`) generated from the repo's markdown: home dashboard with roadmap progress per milestone, latest changes and build commit; \"How to test\" guide; offline search. `tools/publish-pages.sh` publishes it with the viewer (under `/app/`) and a synthetic test bundle to the `gh-pages` branch; `tools/make-test-bundle.mjs` writes a synthetic `*.bikecapture.zip`. The Actions-based `pages.yml` deploy is removed. (#4)"],[37,"Does `PhotogrammetrySession.Poses` return camera→model transforms in the same frame as the\nUSDZ? (Assumed, and the photo close-ups depend on it; validate by checking that an area's top\nclose-up really shows that area on a real capture.)"],[193,"DOM code (`ui/dom.ts`, `viewer/pins.ts`, `ui/photoViewer.ts`, `ui/photoLibrary.ts`,\n`ui/photoDecode.ts`) opts into happy-dom with a first-line comment\n`// @vitest-environment happy-dom`. Browser APIs happy-dom lacks are stubbed per test:\n`createImageBitmap`, `<img>.decode`, `OffscreenCanvas`, `Worker` (photoDecode), pointer capture\n(lightbox gestures), a fake `Viewer` (pins). Decoding itself is mocked in `photoLibrary.test.ts`."],[75,"Drop a `.bikecapture.zip` from the iPhone app (or a `.glb`, `.usdz`, `.ply`) onto the viewer to use your own capture. Switch to **Edit** to\ntap the bike and add comments, save camera views as areas; **Present** steps through areas for\na customer."],[182,"End-to-end tests"],[44,"Every PR adds a line under **Unreleased** (newest first) with its PR number. When the owner\nmerges the stack to `main`, the Unreleased block becomes a dated release."],[226,"Everything else goes through the real UI: clicks, taps, keys, the file picker\n(`setInputFiles`), real `DragEvent` drops with a `DataTransfer`, dialogs and downloads. Keep the\nhook read-mostly; if a test needs to mutate app state through it, that is a sign a UI path is\nmissing."],[197,"Excluded from coverage in `apps/web/vite.config.ts`, each covered by the E2E suite instead:"],[11,"Fallbacks when Object Capture struggles with a bike (thin spokes are the classic failure):\narea mode + a crop box, or a gaussian splat (Scaniverse/Polycam/Luma) for photoreal paint.\nThe green background mode exists for compositing snapshots/videos in other tools."],[224,"find a point on the model to tap: `modelPoint()` in `e2e/helpers.ts` asks the app's own\n`viewer.pick()` and checks `document.elementFromPoint` so the tap lands on the canvas, not a pin;"],[179,"Fixtures"],[190,"Fixtures for both come from one generator: `tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`."],[209,"Folding the three JS generators into one is a ROADMAP follow-up."],[33,"For the active area (its view target, preferring cameras on the side its saved view looks from),\nthe active comment (its pin, preferring cameras in front of its surface normal) and each Present\nstep, the viewer shows a filmstrip of the capture photos that best show that point; tapping one\nopens a full-screen viewer (arrows / swipe, pinch / wheel / double-tap zoom, Esc)."],[51,"Foundation: three.js viewer/editor with areas, pinned sales comments, present mode, background modes, `bike-scene/1` format; iOS Object Capture app skeleton; CI. (#1)"],[204,"Four generators, each with a job. All output is synthetic; no real capture is ever committed."],[53,"Goals"],[166,"How the automated tests work and how to add them: Testing."],[151,"How to test"],[96,"Ideas parking lot"],[17,"Importing in the browser (`apps/web/src/scene/capture.ts`): dropping a `*.bikecapture.zip`\nunzips it in memory with fflate; nothing is uploaded. The iOS exporter zips its staging folder\n(`NSFileCoordinator .forUploading`), so files usually sit under one top-level directory: the\nshallowest `manifest.json` defines the bundle root and `__MACOSX/` / `._*` entries are ignored.\nOnly `manifest.json`, the model and `poses.json` are decompressed (size-capped); images are just\nlisted. If `manifest.model` is missing, a `glb`/`gltf`/`usdz`/`ply` next to the manifest is used\n(GLB first, e.g. after `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`). A broken `poses.json` is a warning, not an error."],[106,"iOS app skeleton: Object Capture (object + area mode), on-device reconstruction, poses, bundle export"],[168,"It writes a low-poly bike as `model.glb`, a `manifest.json`, an orbit of camera poses in\n`poses.json` and no photos, all nested in one folder like the real export. Drag the file onto\nthe viewer (or use **Open…**). Dropping the same file again later restores the comments you\nadded to it."],[154,"Make a synthetic capture bundle"],[78,"Manual steps"],[98,"Markers: `[ ]` open · `[~]` in progress (draft PR open) · `[x]` done (in an open or merged PR)."],[149,"Measure tool (tap two points → distance in mm)."],[31,"Measured on a synthetic 23 MB USDZ (972k triangles, 2048² texture; `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py\n--detail 90 --tex 2048`), Chromium: unzip 16 ms, parse 183 ms, build 206 ms, textures 24 ms. Parsing\nstays on the main thread: a worker would save the ~0.2 s parse but pay ~0.07 s structured-clone of\nthe spec table back, and the build step needs three.js objects on the main thread anyway. The USD\ncode (~70 KB min) is a lazy chunk loaded on the first USDZ. Anything that still fails shows an error\npointing to `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`. Fixtures are synthetic (`apps/web/test/fixtures/README.md`)."],[89,"Milestone 0: Project ops"],[90,"Milestone 1: Foundation (PR 1)"],[91,"Milestone 2: Real captures into the viewer"],[92,"Milestone 3: Sales experience"],[93,"Milestone 4: iOS app depth"],[94,"Milestone 5: Backend & multi-bike catalog"],[95,"Milestone 6: Quality"],[227,"Never `waitForTimeout`. Wait on app state (`waitForFunction`, `expect.poll`) or on web-first\nassertions (`toHaveText`, `toHaveCount`, `toHaveAttribute`)."],[57,"Non-goals (for now)"],[26,"Object Capture writes a USDZ whose root layer is **binary USDC (crate)**: one baked triangle\nmesh, indexed face-varying `primvars:st` and normals, a `UsdPreviewSurface` fed by\n`UsdUVTexture` PNGs in `0/` (diffuse, normal with scale 2 / bias -1, occlusion),\n`metersPerUnit = 1`, `upAxis = \"Y\"`."],[153,"On a laptop"],[232,"On CI a failing run uploads `playwright-report/` and `test-results/` (traces, screenshots) as\nthe `playwright-report` artifact. CI retries once; a test that only passes on retry is reported\nas flaky and should be fixed, not ignored."],[152,"On your phone (no setup)"],[9,"Open questions (verify on device)"],[157,"Open the live demo: **https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/**\n(this site lives one level up: https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/)."],[71,"Overview"],[8,"Photo close-ups"],[46,"Photo close-ups: for the active area, the active comment and each Present step, a filmstrip of the capture photos that best show it (ranked from `poses.json`), with a full-screen viewer (swipe, arrows, pinch/zoom). Photos are read lazily from the zip, HEIC is decoded natively or by a lazily loaded WASM worker, and thumbnails are kept in the capture cache. (#6)"],[220,"Playwright drives the **production build** (`vite build` + `vite preview` on port 4190, started\nby the config's `webServer`) in two projects: `desktop` (1280×800, every spec) and `mobile`\n(iPhone 14 viewport with touch, DPR 1 to keep CPU rendering fast; only the specs where layout and\ntouch matter: view, edit, present, photos). WebGL runs on SwiftShader\n(`--use-angle=swiftshader --enable-unsafe-swiftshader`), so no GPU is needed. CI splits the\nsuite into two parallel shards (`--shard=1/2`, `2/2`)."],[105,"Procedural demo bike with seeded areas and comments"],[54,"Product"],[86,"Progress"],[68,"Public release / app store distribution (the owner decides when)."],[64,"Pure logic in `apps/web/src/scene/` with unit tests; coverage does not go down."],[191,"Pure logic lives in `apps/web/src/scene/` (scene format, store, camera math, capture bundles,\nUI helpers in `helpers.ts`) and is tested in plain Node. When UI code grows a decision (a\ndefault, a message, a URL rule), move it into `src/scene/helpers.ts` and test it there."],[56,"Quality bar for every PR"],[225,"read the scene for assertions (`store.scene`)."],[69,"Real customer captures in the repo: only generated fixtures."],[181,"Rendered-photo bundle"],[88,"Roadmap"],[87,"Roadmap status per milestone, generated from ROADMAP.md at build time."],[103,"Scene format `bike-scene/1` with validation, local persistence, import/export"],[230,"Screenshots are for humans: `snap(page, testInfo, name)` saves to `test-results/` and attaches\nto the HTML report. Do not add pixel-diff assertions; SwiftShader output differs across\nmachines."],[32,"See `apps/web/src/scene/schema.ts`. A scene references its model by URL (relative to the\nscene file), lists **hotspots** (named camera views: the zoomable areas) and **annotations**\n(surface point + normal, title, body, kind `feature|spec|upgrade|note`, optional price and area).\nAll coordinates are in model-root space."],[76,"See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, ROADMAP.md and\napps/ios/README.md. Inspired by\nwesbos/3d-model-anything."],[148,"Size guide overlay (rider silhouette to scale)."],[19,"So a capture scene survives a reload, every successfully opened bundle is kept in the browser\n(`apps/web/src/scene/captureCache.ts`, pure logic; `apps/web/src/storage/backends.ts`, storage):"],[194,"Storage: `storage/backends.ts` runs against `fake-indexeddb` and a small in-memory OPFS\n(`FakeDir` in `backends.test.ts`); `navigator` is replaced with `vi.stubGlobal`."],[55,"Success criteria"],[45,"Test system: Playwright E2E suite (`npm run e2e`, desktop + iPhone viewport, sharded CI job) over the production build, covering every viewer flow including stored captures, photo close-ups and binary USDC; synthetic capture-bundle fixtures (`tools/fixtures/make-capture-bundle.mjs`, rendered-photo bundle via `render-photos.mjs`); unit coverage with ratcheting thresholds (`npm run test:coverage`, ~99.8% lines) incl. zip64 parsing, OPFS/IndexedDB backends and the photo UI; `docs/TESTING.md`. UI decisions moved into tested `scene/helpers.ts`; `?e2e` test hook. Fixed: a tap right after an instant (reduced-motion) fly-to missed the model. (#7)"],[175,"Testing"],[231,"Tests run in parallel across fresh browser contexts, so each test starts from an empty\n`localStorage` and the seeded demo."],[183,"The `window.__bike` test hook"],[162,"The background buttons switch between clear, chroma green, studio and dark."],[97,"The backlog autonomous sessions work through, top to bottom. Each item is sized for one\nsession / one PR. Protocol is in CLAUDE.md."],[219,"The E2E global setup (`apps/web/e2e/global-setup.ts`) also renders the `make-capture.mjs` bike\nfrom each of its poses with `render-photos.mjs` (headless Chromium, three.js, the iPhone wide\ncamera's field of view) and writes `bike-photos.bikecapture.zip`, so photo close-ups are ranked\nand shown from real images of the fixture."],[167,"The iPhone app exports `*.bikecapture.zip` (format `bike-capture/1`, see\nArchitecture). To test the import path without a phone:"],[218,"The photos are PNG stand-ins: real captures have HEIC, which Node cannot encode."],[158,"The procedural demo bike loads with sample areas and comments."],[18,"The resulting scene gets a stable id (`capture-<name>-<createdAt digits>`) so dropping the same\nbundle again restores its saved areas and comments, and a model URL `bundle:<zip name>/<path>`,\nwhich is never fetched: it is resolved from memory or from the capture cache below, and only\nwhen neither has it does the viewer ask for that zip to be dropped again."],[164,"The site is redeployed by `tools/publish-pages.sh` after each finished PR, so it shows the\nnewest work in the stack, which may not be merged yet. The footer of the home page says which\ncommit and branch it was built from."],[79,"Things an agent cannot do (hardware, accounts, decisions). Newest first."],[186,"Three layers, cheapest first. CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs all of them on every PR."],[192,"three.js code that needs no WebGL (loaders, `centerOnGround`, the demo bike's geometry) is\ntested in Node too (`viewer-node.test.ts`). three's `FileLoader` needs a `ProgressEvent`\nstub in Node; the test file installs one. Models are passed as `data:` URLs."],[27,"three.js r186 can read this: `USDLoader` (the old `USDZLoader` is a deprecated alias) has a crate\nparser with LZ4 + integer decoding (`usd/USDCParser.js`) and a composer that handles xforms,\nGeomSubsets, indexed/face-varying primvars, UsdPreviewSurface textures, `metersPerUnit` and Z-up.\nWe reuse those parsers and patch what fails on real-world files:"],[163,"To try a capture bundle without the iPhone app, download the synthetic one:\n**https://davidpn11.github.io/bike-3d-brew/app/samples/synthetic-bike.bikecapture.zip**,\nthen in the viewer tap **Open…** and pick it from Files. A red low-poly bike replaces the demo\nand the scene is named \"Synthetic test bike\"."],[66,"UI changes verified in Chromium with screenshots, at desktop and phone sizes."],[176,"Unit tests"],[42,"Unreleased"],[196,"USD: `usdz.test.ts` loads the committed binary USDC fixtures (`apps/web/test/fixtures/`, made\nby `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py` with Pixar USD); `usd-units.test.ts` drives the crate\ndecoders and composer fast paths directly for encodings the fixtures do not contain."],[6,"USDZ loading (`apps/web/src/viewer/usd/`)"],[49,"USDZ robustness: Object Capture USDZ (binary USDC) loads with textures; fixes three.js r186 crate decoding of inline vectors/halves/negative ints, ~10× faster mesh build for large captures, lazy-loaded USD code, clear fallback to `tools/usdz-to-glb.py`. Synthetic fixture generator `tools/fixtures/make-usdc.py`. (#3)"],[229,"Use `collectErrors(page)` and assert it is empty where a flow should be clean."],[223,"wait for state instead of sleeping: `ready` (boot finished), a model in `viewer.modelRoot`,\n`viewer.flying` (camera animation running);"],[102,"Web viewer: three.js, orbit, fly-to areas, background modes (clear / chroma green / studio / dark)"],[155,"What each PR adds"],[177,"What is not unit-tested, and why"],[185,"What the suite covers"],[2,"Why Object Capture instead of Wes Bos' room pipeline"],[169,"With a real capture: AirDrop the `.bikecapture.zip` from the iPhone to the laptop and drop it on\nthe viewer. If the model does not show, note what the viewer says and add it to\nManual steps."],[184,"Writing reliable E2E tests"],[195,"Zip parsing: `zipIndex.test.ts` hand-builds zips byte by byte (zip64 records and extra fields,\nforeign extras, odd methods, lying sizes), branches fflate never writes."]],"type":"string"},"page_id":{"docs":{"1":7,"2":8,"3":9,"4":10,"5":11,"6":12,"7":13,"8":14,"9":15,"10":16,"11":17,"12":18,"13":19,"14":20,"15":21,"16":22,"17":23,"18":24,"19":25,"20":26,"21":27,"22":28,"23":29,"24":30,"25":31,"26":32,"27":33,"28":34,"29":35,"30":36,"31":37,"32":38,"33":39,"34":40,"35":41,"36":42,"37":43,"38":44,"39":45,"40":46,"41":47,"42":48,"43":49,"44":50,"45":51,"46":52,"47":53,"48":54,"49":55,"50":56,"51":57,"52":58,"53":59,"54":60,"55":61,"56":62,"57":63,"58":64,"59":65,"60":66,"61":67,"62":68,"63":69,"64":70,"65":71,"66":72,"67":73,"68":74,"69":75,"70":76,"71":0,"72":1,"73":2,"74":3,"75":4,"76":5,"77":6,"78":77,"79":78,"80":79,"81":80,"82":81,"83":82,"84":83,"85":84,"86":85,"87":86,"88":87,"89":88,"90":89,"91":90,"92":91,"93":92,"94":93,"95":94,"96":95,"97":96,"98":97,"99":98,"100":99,"101":100,"102":101,"103":102,"104":103,"105":104,"106":105,"107":106,"108":10